173	**How the verdict was reached:** `implemented` applies because enforcement is present and was followed through the arithmetic callee. `Math.mulDiv(grossPot, 500, 10_000)` computes the floor of one calculation over the accumulated `unsettledPot` (`Raffle.sol:L539-L540`; `RaffleConstants.sol:L11-L15`; `Math.sol:L199-L275`). It is not `partial`: both fee-bearing outcomes execute that same calculation before branching, both callable settlement routes converge on the same private function, and both outcome branches define sponsor proceeds by exact subtraction from `grossPot` (`Raffle.sol:L303-L318`, `L533-L555`). It is not `contradicted`: no ceiling, per-purchase fee sum, or discarded residual appears in the scoped writers and callers, while each branch's stored liabilities algebraically sum to the original pot (`Raffle.sol:L539-L555`). The separate floor applied to the cash-winner share does not change this verdict; the sponsor subtraction absorbs its residual as well (`Raffle.sol:L546-L548`). This is the exact requested behavior, not an additional restriction, so `stronger-than-spec` does not apply.
